;; FH-STRUCT-007 — the React emitter puts real DOM on a real page.
;;
;; The structural rows prove what the tree SAYS. This one proves what the
;; browser DOES, because an element tree is not a rendered page: an
;; emitter can produce a perfectly shaped `createElement` call for an
;; attribute name React declines to set, a class React drops, or a child
;; React reorders, and no amount of element-tree assertion would notice.
;; So the assertions below are read off `document`, after a real
;; `react-dom/client` mount, against the SAME declaration FH-STRUCT-006
;; renders structurally.
;;
;; Each `:dom` row is one query and what must be true of its result:
;;
;;   :selector  a CSS selector, resolved inside the mounted container
;;   :tag       the matched element's tagName
;;   :text      its textContent
;;   :attrs     attribute name -> value, read with getAttribute
;;   :count     how many elements the selector matches (with :selector-all)
{:fh/id "FH-STRUCT-007"
 :fh/law
 "The interpreted React emitter mounts a declared view as real DOM: elements, converted attribute names, composed classes, text, and a keyed run of child boundaries."

 :view  :page
 :props {:items [1 2 3]}

 :dom
 [{:note "the root element is the tag the declaration names, with its sugar id"
   :selector "#main" :tag "SECTION"}

  {:note "sugar classes and the truthy flag-map entries compose into one className"
   :selector "#main" :attrs {"class" "panel open" "id" "main"}}

  {:note "the kebab attribute name reaches the DOM in its collapsed spelling"
   :selector "#main" :attrs {"tabindex" "3"}}

  {:note "a false flag-map entry contributes no class"
   :selector-all "#main.busy" :count 0}

  {:note "static text renders as text, in its own element"
   :selector "#main > h2" :text "Details"}

  {:note "the run of child view boundaries renders one element per item, in order"
   :selector-all "ul.rows > li.row" :count 3}

  {:note "each child boundary renders its own props — numbers as text"
   :selector "ul.rows > li.row" :text "1"}

  {:note "the whole subtree's text is the document-order concatenation"
   :selector "#main" :text "Details123"}]}
